  "description": "Terrain repairs the polls of a stream gap after the drive has ended. D wire frames start the drive with the frame's elevation (30, 32); between them a single D poll stays without elevation. Then the stream sends no D/N/R frame while D polls keep coming at distinct coordinates: the first two polls after the last stream position are stored without elevation and not looked up, from the third on the lookup at insert cannot answer (one unavailable lookup each), so those polls are stored without elevation too, and the P poll closes the drive with an ascent of 2 and a descent of 0 from the stream positions alone. Every coordinate, the parked car position included, has a declared terrain elevation. The elevation repair then runs one Terrain pass: from the third poll after the last stream position on, the polls get the terrain elevation (61, 58, 70) and the drive's ascent (43) and descent (3) are recomputed with the gap; the first two gap polls, the single poll between the frames and the car positions keep no elevation. Ends asleep so the replay stays repeat-neutral; the asleep terminal is reached from :online and is therefore awaited.",
